@attribute [Route(LegalPages.Privacy)]
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@* The privacy policy the identity server's sign-in page for Beep Oil & Gas links (LegalPages). Public: a person reads it
   before creating an account, so it carries no authorization requirement and the layout's setup gate lets it through.
   Every statement describes what this application and its API actually do — the account the API provisions
   (RepositoryBootstrapService, RepositoryCanonicalUserStore), the access decisions it records
   (AuthorizationObservabilityService), the failure store and its 90-day window (TheTechIdeaWeb.Diagnostics), the
   identity client library's cookies and session token store, the theme choice in local storage (ThemeState), Google Fonts
   (App.razor), and deletion switching the account off (OilGasAccountDeactivation). When one of those changes, this page
   changes with it. English only, as the application is. *@

<PageTitle>Privacy policy - Beep Oil &amp; Gas</PageTitle>

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Medium" Class="py-6">
    <MudPaper Outlined="true" Class="pa-6">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" HtmlTag="h1">Privacy policy</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mb-4">
            Effective @LegalPages.EffectiveDateText
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
            This policy explains what personal data Beep Oil &amp; Gas holds when you use it, why it holds it, who else
            receives it, how long it is kept, and how to get a copy or have it removed. Every statement describes what the
            application actually does.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Who is responsible</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            Beep Oil &amp; Gas is provided by @LegalPages.Operator, which runs this site, the API service behind it and their
            databases, and is responsible for the personal data described here. Privacy questions and requests:
            <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.ContactHref">@LegalPages.ContactEmail</MudLink>.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            Beep Oil &amp; Gas is a business application. The operational, engineering and financial records in it belong to
            the organization they are entered for, and that organization decides what goes into them — including any personal
            data they contain, such as the name of a lessor, a royalty owner, a contractor or a person involved in an
            incident. We hold and process those records so the application can work.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">What we hold, and why</MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" HtmlTag="h3" Class="mt-4 mb-1">Your sign-in</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            Signing in and creating an account happen at @LegalPages.Operator's identity service,
            <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.IdentityService" Target="_blank">@LegalPages.IdentityServiceName</MudLink>, which holds
            your email address, your password or the external provider you sign in with, and your two-factor and passkey
            settings. Beep Oil &amp; Gas never sees your password. When you sign in, the identity service gives this site your
            account identifier there, your name, your email address and whether it has been verified, and issues the tokens
            this site uses to call its API service as you.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" HtmlTag="h3" Class="mt-4 mb-1">Your Beep Oil &amp; Gas account</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-1">The first time you sign in, the API service creates an account for you. It holds:</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Badge" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Your account identifier, and the identity service's identifier for you, which links the two.</MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Person" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    Your name, and your email address once the identity service has verified it — both kept up to date from the
                    identity service as you use the site.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ToggleOn" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Whether the account is active, and when you last signed in.</MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.AdminPanelSettings" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    The roles an administrator gives you, with who granted each, why and from when, and the fields, wells and
                    other assets you may reach.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Tune" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    Your workspace settings: the persona you chose, your default field, locale, time zone, unit system, layout
                    and saved view preferences, with a history of persona changes.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            We hold this to sign you in, to give you exactly the access your administrators assign, and to keep a record of
            who was given what access.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" HtmlTag="h3" Class="mt-4 mb-1">The records you work with</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            The fields, wells, wellbores, production volumes, facilities, prospects, seismic surveys, leases, permits, work
            orders, HSE incidents, approvals, accounting and royalty records and the calculations you save are stored by the
            API service, together with the files you import into them. Each record notes who created it, who last changed it
            and when. Workflow tasks assigned to you, the approvals you give and the notifications the application shows you
            are kept with your account identifier. These records name people whenever you or your colleagues enter people's
            names in them.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            We hold this because it is what the application is for, and the record of who changed what is what makes
            engineering and financial records trustworthy.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" HtmlTag="h3" Class="mt-4 mb-1">Security and fault records</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Security" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    When the API service decides whether a request may reach a protected record, it records the decision: your
                    account identifier, the record, the permission asked for, the outcome, the time and the network address the
                    request came from.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ReportProblem" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    When something goes wrong, the site and the API service record what was being attempted, the technical
                    detail of the error, the address of the request and the reference you are shown, so an administrator can
                    find and fix the problem.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Article" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    Both keep server logs of requests and events for troubleshooting. These can include your account
                    identifier, for example where a request was refused.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Logout" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    When you sign out at the identity service, it tells this site, which keeps your identity-service identifier
                    and the time, so that a sign-in cookie issued before then cannot be used again.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Who else receives it</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.VpnKey" IconColor="Color.Secondary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>The identity service.</b> Run by @LegalPages.Operator at @LegalPages.IdentityServiceName; it holds your
                    sign-in and confirms who you are each time you sign in. If you sign in there with an external provider, that
                    provider takes part in signing you in.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Groups" IconColor="Color.Secondary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Your colleagues and administrators.</b> People using Beep Oil &amp; Gas see records according to the
                    roles and asset access administrators give them. Administrators also see accounts, roles, access decisions
                    and fault records.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.FontDownload" IconColor="Color.Secondary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Google Fonts.</b> Pages load their typeface from Google's font service, so your browser sends Google
                    its network address and browser details when a page loads. Apart from the identity service while you sign
                    in, it is the only outside service your browser contacts from these pages.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Dns" IconColor="Color.Secondary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Our hosting provider.</b> The site, the API service and their databases run on servers our hosting
                    provider operates for us, which store this data on our behalf.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            Beep Oil &amp; Gas sends no email or text messages of its own: messages about your account — confirming your
            address, resetting your password, security notices — come from the identity service. We do not sell personal
            data, and we do not share it with advertisers or data brokers.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Cookies and browser storage</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-1">This site sets only the cookies it needs to work, so there is nothing to opt in to:</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Lock" IconColor="Color.Secondary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>A sign-in cookie</b>, which keeps you signed in. It lapses after 14 days without use, never outlasts
                    your sign-in at the identity service, and ends when you sign out.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.VerifiedUser" IconColor="Color.Secondary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Sign-in check cookies</b>, set only while a sign-in is under way, so this site can tell that the
                    answer coming back from the identity service is the one your browser asked for.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Shield" IconColor="Color.Secondary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>An anti-forgery cookie</b>, which stops another site submitting forms — signing out, for example — as you.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            The tokens the identity service issues for your session are kept on this site's server, not in your browser,
            encrypted, and for no more than 14 days after they were last used. Your choice of light or dark appearance is kept
            in your browser's local storage and is never sent to us. There are no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">How long we keep it</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Badge" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Your Beep Oil &amp; Gas account</b> is kept for as long as the service runs. Deleting your account
                    switches it off rather than erasing it, because the records you created, changed or approved refer to it
                    and must stay attributable.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Inventory" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Business records</b> are kept until someone with permission deletes them. Some kinds of record are only
                    marked inactive when deleted, so that the history they belong to stays intact.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Security" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Access decisions</b> are kept as the security history of the records they protect; they are not
                    removed automatically.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ReportProblem" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1"><b>Fault records</b> are kept for 90 days.</MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Timer" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Sign-out records</b> are kept for 14 days, and session tokens for no more than 14 days after they were
                    last used.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Article" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1"><b>Server logs</b> are kept on the server for troubleshooting.</MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Your rights, and how to use them</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Edit" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>See and correct your details.</b> Your name and email address come from your identity-service account.
                    Change them on the Profile tab of <MudLink Href="@BeepClientEndpoints.Manage">your account page</MudLink>,
                    and this site picks up the change the next time you use it.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Download" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Get a copy.</b> The Personal Data tab of your account page downloads what the identity service holds
                    about you. It does not include what Beep Oil &amp; Gas holds: for a copy of your account record, roles and
                    settings, and of the records that name you, write to <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.ContactHref">@LegalPages.ContactEmail</MudLink>.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.PersonRemove" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Delete your account.</b> The same tab deletes your sign-in account at the identity service, switches your
                    Beep Oil &amp; Gas account off, and then asks you to sign out to finish. If you are the only active
                    administrator, you are asked to make someone else an administrator first. Your Beep Oil &amp; Gas account
                    record — including your name and email address — and the records you created stay, as part of your
                    organization's engineering and financial history. To ask what remains, or to ask for your name and email
                    address to be removed from it, write to us.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ContactSupport" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    <b>Anything else</b> — including objecting to how we use your data, or asking about records someone else
                    entered that name you — write to <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.ContactHref">@LegalPages.ContactEmail</MudLink>.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Changes to this policy</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            The date at the top is when this version took effect. If the policy changes, that date changes with it, and
            continuing to use Beep Oil &amp; Gas after a change means the updated policy applies. How the service itself may be
            used is set out in our <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.Terms">terms of service</MudLink>.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Contact</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
            Questions about this policy or your data: <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.ContactHref">@LegalPages.ContactEmail</MudLink>.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>
</MudContainer>
